{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender mathutils Extension.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender mathutils Extension.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender mathutils extension blender mathutils extension","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender mathutils Extension.md","fileName":"Blender mathutils Extension.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender mathutils Extension","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-14 00:20\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Blender Embedded Python Internals]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Embedded Python Internals","Blender blenlib Module","Blender mathutils VectorObject","Blender mathutils Vector Construction","Blender mathutils Vector Method Dispatch","coreblenderdevelopment.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender mathutils Extension.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender mathutils Extension.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender mathutils extension blender mathutils extension","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender mathutils Extension.md","fileName":"Blender mathutils Extension.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender mathutils Extension","heading":"Blender mathutils Extension","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"`mathutils` is a built-in Blender Python extension that presents mathematical objects such as vectors, matrices, quaternions, and colors as Python classes. Its methods reuse low-level mathematical functions from the [[Blender blenlib Module]] without requiring RNA for every object.\n\nThe extension provides a compact example of the complete CPython bridge. [[Blender mathutils VectorObject]] defines instance storage, [[Blender mathutils Vector Construction]] allocates it, and [[Blender mathutils Vector Method Dispatch]] connects script-visible operations to C functions.","tags